MILESTONE 1: Model Selection and Architecture – LegalEase 
In this milestone, we focus on selecting the optimal generative AI model for creating 
personalized and accurate legal documents using Google’s Gemini model via the Google 
Generative AI SDK. We also define the system architecture and set up the development 
environment to support document generation, editing, and exporting in various formats 
(.docx, .pdf, .txt). 
Activity 1.1: Research and Select the Appropriate Generative AI Model 
1. Understand the Project Requirements 
o LegalEase must generate structured legal documents (e.g., contracts, 
NDAs, agreements) based on user inputs such as: 
 Document type 
 Parties involved 
 Terms and conditions 
 Effective dates 
2. Explore Gemini Model Documentation 
o Visit Google Generative AI Documentation to evaluate available Gemini 
models. 
o Review capabilities of gemini-1.5-pro, especially: 
 Long context window (up to 1 million tokens) 
 Structured prompting with multi-part content 
 Fast generation speed and legal-domain compatibility 
3. Evaluate Model Performance 
o Benchmarks indicate that gemini-1.5-pro is capable of handling complex 
formatting, reasoning, and structured text generation, making it suitable 
for legal content generation. 
4. Select the Optimal Model 
Selected: gemini-1.5-pro 
 Best suited for drafting formal documents with clear sections and 
legal jargon. 
 Capable of understanding and generating clauses based on user 
inputs dynamically. 
Activity 1.2: Define the Architecture of the Application 
1. Architectural Diagram 
 Components: 
o Frontend: Streamlit for user interaction (document input, preview, 
editing, downloads) 
o Backend: FastAPI app (routes input to Gemini model and returns 
generated content) 
o AI Core: Gemini integration for content generation 
o Formatting Modules: DOCX, PDF, TXT generators 
2. Frontend Functionality 
 Users provide inputs via: 
o TextInput for document type and dates 
o TextArea for parties and terms 
 Buttons: 
o "Generate Document" 
o "Edit Document" 
o "Download as TXT / DOCX / PDF" 
 Styled HTML preview of the generated legal document 
3. Backend Responsibilities 
 Expose POST /generate endpoint (via FastAPI) 
 Accept JSON input (document_type, parties, terms, dates) 
 Route to GeminiDocumentGenerator 
 Return structured document text 
4. AI Integration Points 
 GeminiDocumentGenerator forms a structured prompt and sends it to Gemini via 
generate_content 
 Receives generated text and returns to FastAPI 
 Frontend displays and allows editing or exporting 
Activity 1.3: Set Up the Development Environment 
1. Install Python and Pip 
Ensure Python 3.10+ is installed along with pip for dependency management. 
2. Create a Virtual Environment 
3. Install FastAPI and Uvicorn (Backend Server) 
pip install fastapi uvicorn 
4. Install Streamlit (Frontend UI) 
pip install streamlit 
5. Install Google Generative AI SDK 
pip install google-generativeai 
6. Install Additional Libraries 
pip install python-docx fpdf Pillow requests python-dotenv 
7.  Set Up Application Structure         
MILESTONE 2: Core Functionalities Development 
Activity 2.1: Develop the core functionalities 
1. Legal Document Generation  
Functionality: Generate legal documents (e.g., contracts, agreements) based on user 
inputs (document type, parties, terms, and dates). 
2. Document Output Formatting  
Functionality: Convert raw AI-generated text into structured .docx, .pdf, .txt files with 
legal formatting, logos, tables, and footers. 
 format_docx(text, doc_type) 
 format_pdf(text, doc_type) 
 format_html_preview(text) 
These use: 
 docx for Microsoft Word formatting (includes logo, Times New Roman font, 
terms as table, footer). 
 fpdf for clean, branded PDF documents with headers/footers. 
 HTML Preview with Streamlit styling. 
3. User Interaction & Recommendations  
Functionality: Accept user preferences through the Streamlit interface and reflect them 
in the AI-generated legal content. 
4. Editable Document & Download  
Functionality: Provides editable text area, allows download in .txt, .docx, .pdf formats. 
