Exploring LegalEase 
1. Document Type 
Purpose: Type of legal document to generate. 
Examples: 
 Agreement 
 Contract 
 NDA (Non-Disclosure Agreement) 
 Lease Agreement 
 Employment Offer Letter 
Example input: Freelance Work Contract 
2. Parties Involved 
Purpose: Names and roles of the individuals or entities involved in the document. 
Examples: 
 John Doe (Freelancer), ABC Corp (Client) 
 Alice Smith (Tenant), XYZ Realty (Landlord) 
Example input: Jane Doe (Service Provider), TechNova Inc. (Client) 
3. Terms & Conditions (Use semicolons for bullet points) 
Purpose: Specific clauses or rules that define the agreement. Separate each bullet point 
using a semicolon. 
Examples: 
 Payment to be made within 30 days of invoice; 
 The provider agrees to deliver work by the agreed deadline; 
 Confidentiality must be maintained at all times; 
 Either party may terminate with 15 days notice 
4. Effective Date 
Purpose: The date when the agreement becomes legally valid. 
Examples: 
 April 10, 2025 
 10/04/2025 
 April 15, 2025 
 
Document Generated 
 
